course: dictionary
lesson: 12362
title: Croaked: a sound and a slang word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Croaked is a verb, a word for an action. Its first meaning is a sound: a deep, rough noise, like a frog at the pond or a person whose throat is sore. «The frog croaked by the pond all night.» You can hear it in your head, and that is a good sign you have the right meaning.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so context must decide. Read the words around croaked. A pond, a frog or a sore throat points to the sound. «In the crime film, the villain croaked in the last scene» points to a slang meaning: died. Slang is rough and jokey, and it is never polite, so do not use it in school or with friends.
explain: To check, swap your meaning into the sentence. «The frog made a deep, rough sound all night» still makes sense. For the slang sense, the sentence would still need the crime-film clues around it, so the story tells you which one it is.
fact: «Croaked» means made a deep, rough sound, like a frog or a person with a sore throat.
fact: Croak is a verb. Its forms are croak, croaks, croaked and croaking.
fact: «Croaked» can also be slang for died. It is rough and jokey, and you will mostly find it in crime stories, films and dark humour.
fact: Slang is informal talk. The slang meaning of croaked is never polite, so use the sound meaning in ordinary speech and writing.
fact: Context tells you which meaning is right: a pond or sore throat means the sound, while a crime film or villain may mean the slang.
exercise: «The frog croaked by the pond all night.» What does croaked mean here? | *Made a deep, rough sound, like a frog | Sang a sweet tune | Jumped high into the air | Ran very fast
exercise: «Her voice croaked after she had cheered all day at the match.» What does croaked describe? | *A rough, hoarse sound from a sore throat | A quiet whisper | A splash in the water | A loud, happy song
exercise: In a crime film, a character says, «He croaked in the last scene.» What does croaked mean in this slang? | Shouted for help | *Died, in rough, jokey slang that is never polite | Fell fast asleep | Was spotted by the police
test: Find and copy the verb that means made a rough sound: «The old crow croaked and flew off the fence.» | crow | flew | *croaked | fence
test: «Croak» changes when we talk about the past. Which form is the past tense? | croaking | croak | *croaked | croaks
exam: Your friend reads «The frog croaked» and then «The villain croaked». How can you tell which meaning is which? | Both always mean the same thing | *Look at the words around it: a pond means the sound, and a crime film means the slang | Ask someone to shout the word | Guess from the first letter of each word
